  "body": "First slice of #1468. Fork synced from `upstream/main` at 31f8d03d7 (branch cut from it, not from a tag). Not stacked: no open PR changes these files except the camcraft-mcp skill (#1738, #1817, #2037 edit other rows).\n\n## What changed\n\n- **Dialog: \"Fit to the stock\" for a lathe chuck.** \"Add accessory…\" shows a **Fit to the stock** checkbox for the 3-jaw, 4-jaw and collet chuck. Ticked, Place queues `InsertAccessory` with the existing `OnStock` placement; the grip diameter (or collet bore) is shown as \"(set by the fit)\" and disabled, and the pose rows give way to a line that says what the fit does. The box opens ticked when the setup's stock reads as round.\n- **Inside grip** (`JawChuck::grip`, `outside` | `inside`). An inside jaw runs inward from the grip diameter; its gripping face is the arc of the bore it opens into, drawn circumscribed (flats on the grip circle, steps of at most 1/256 turn), so the drawn steel is never less than the jaw.\n- **Stepped jaws** (`step_height`, `step_depth`; both 0 for plain jaws). Below the step height the jaw reaches the step depth past the gripping face, under the work. A stock fit seats the stock on the step: the chuck's face goes the step height below the stock's underside.\n- **Refusals by name** (all in `camcraft_sim::chuck::jaw::check`): a step figure that is not finite, negative or over 5000 mm; one step figure without the other; a step as tall as its jaw; a step or an inside jaw that reaches the axis; steps or inside jaws that would meet each other; an inside jaw wider than its bore, shorter than its own arc, or past the body. A stock fit with an inside grip is refused (\"an inside grip opens into the work's bore, which the stock's box does not give\"); the dialog unticks and disables the box for an inside grip and says why.\n- **MCP:** `add_accessory` and `set_accessory` take `grip`; the `dimensions` object takes `step_height` and `step_depth`; the result's `accessory` shows `grip` for a jaw chuck. The camcraft-mcp skill row now lists the three chuck kinds, `fit_to_stock`, `grip` and the step figures.\n- **Files:** the three new fields are `serde(default)`, so a project saved before this reads as plain outside jaws, and the default chuck's mesh is unchanged to the triangle (pinned).\n- Guide: `site/content/guide/set-up/workholding.md` describes the chuck rows. Decision record: `docs/decisions/1468-chuck-options.md`.\n\nThe jaw geometry lives in `crates/sim/src/chuck/jaw.rs` (new, with its provenance line); `chuck.rs` keeps the body, the collet and the round-stock read. No new crate dependency.\n\n## Collision consequences (safety floor)\n\nA generated chuck is an ordinary meshed fixture, so the new jaws reach the lathe holder law and the post gate through the same path as #1442:\n\n- `inside_grip_jaws_are_steel_that_blocks_the_post`: a holder whose leg rides through inside-grip jaws is named and the post is blocked; the same holder 2 mm over the jaws posts.\n- `stepped_jaws_are_steel_where_they_stand_under_the_work`: the same for stepped jaws with the face lowered by the step height.\n\n## How tested\n\n`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` on the final head: green (sim, app and ui suites; 3 steps, 0 failed). `cargo clippy -p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\nPinning tests:\n\n- `crates/sim/tests/lathe_chuck_jaws.rs` (new): `outside_stepped_jaw_envelope_is_pinned`, `inside_grip_envelope_is_pinned`, `inside_stepped_jaw_envelope_is_pinned` (steel a hair inside every true face, air a hair past it, outward volume, the drawn arc never inside the true one), `step_nonsense_is_refused_by_name`, `inside_grip_nonsense_is_refused_by_name`, `a_file_from_before_reads_as_plain_outside_jaws`.\n- `crates/app/tests/lathe_chuck.rs`: the two collision tests above and `a_fit_seats_the_stock_on_the_step_and_refuses_an_inside_grip`.\n- `crates/app/tests/mcp_accessory.rs`: `lathe_chucks_are_placed_fitted_to_the_stock_and_undone_over_mcp` (extended: `grip`, step figures, their refusals).\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/fixture_accessory_tests.rs`: `chuck_dialog_offers_fit_to_the_stock`, `chuck_fit_is_off_by_pose_for_an_inside_grip_and_square_stock` (AccessKit labels, toggled and disabled state; no snapshot PNG changed).\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The native GUI window was not launched. The visual evidence below uses the shipping shell and GPU viewport in an offscreen harness.\n- Windows was not tested. Earlier validation ran on macOS. This evidence update uses Linux.\n- Clicking **Inside** in the dialog leaves the generic figures as they are; for the generic 4-jaw (40 mm grip, 50 mm jaws) Place then refuses by name until the grip diameter is typed. No preset is offered for an inside grip.\n\n## Visual evidence for review\n\nBefore: `31f8d03d744e77ce707282d816e11efe0922f239` (the feature commit's parent). After: `a09aef1cd57e1c0abf1083595b27f66f2ec9fe6f`.\n\nThese images use the shipping `shell_layout`, accessory dialog, world scene collector, and `View3D` renderer on Linux.\nAn offscreen egui harness captures the shell. The viewport uses GPU readback. The native GUI window was not launched.\nThe before images use the actual parent source. The after images use the reviewed head source.\nNo image or capture harness is committed to the PR branch.\n\n| View | Before | After |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Add accessory dialog | ![Before: position controls and plain jaws](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/2e69f0e90de3f4167d402c576a7c8e75b7d389b0/2083/dialog-before.png) | ![After: fit controls and step figures](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/2e69f0e90de3f4167d402c576a7c8e75b7d389b0/2083/dialog-fit-after.png) |\n| Inside grip | ![Before: plain outside jaws](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/2e69f0e90de3f4167d402c576a7c8e75b7d389b0/2083/viewport-before.png) | ![After: inside gripping arcs](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/2e69f0e90de3f4167d402c576a7c8e75b7d389b0/2083/viewport-inside-after.png) |\n| Stepped jaws | ![Before: plain outside jaws](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/2e69f0e90de3f4167d402c576a7c8e75b7d389b0/2083/viewport-before.png) | ![After: shelves under the work](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/2e69f0e90de3f4167d402c576a7c8e75b7d389b0/2083/viewport-stepped-after.png) |\n\nThe dialog uses 60 mm round stock. The fit determines the grip diameter when Place runs. The disabled field shows its current draft before placement.\nThe step height is 10 mm and the depth is 8 mm.\nThe inside viewport uses a 100 mm grip diameter and 25 mm radial jaw length. The viewport images hide no jaw steel.\nThe stock is absent from the viewport images so the jaw faces and shelves remain visible.\n\nInside grip disables the stock fit. The dialog explains why the bore requires placement by position:\n\n![After: inside grip, disabled fit, and placement controls](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/2e69f0e90de3f4167d402c576a7c8e75b7d389b0/2083/dialog-inside-after.png)\n\n## What remains on #1468\n\n- Independent 4-jaw offsets (each jaw's own radial position, off-centre work).\n- Chuck rpm limit feeding the workholding spindle-speed checks.\n- Chuck on a rotary axis of a milling setup (frame along the rotary axis).\n- An inside-grip stock fit needs a stock (or part) that states its bore.\n\nChangelog: Lathe chucks: \"Fit to the stock\" in the Add accessory dialog, inside grip and stepped jaws (`grip`, `step_height`, `step_depth`; also over MCP), each refused by name when the figures cannot be built\nEffort: max (no escalation; the issue was escalated from high before this run)\n\nProcess change: yes\n\nRefs #1468\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n\n\n",
